      233:     // Mirror of `batch_index_key_error_aborts_commit` in
      234:     // `crates/vb_storage/src/batch/t_putters_b.rs:177-209` (vb-09aaz).
      235:     //
      236:     // The `append_event` path mirrors the abort-on-error contract used
      237:     // by `put_status_index` / `put_workflow_index` / `put_action_index`
      238:     // in `super::putters`: once a record is staged into the inner
      239:     // `OwnedWriteBatch`, any fallible step that follows — including
      240:     // `stage_pending_action_index_op` — MUST set `self.aborted = true`
      241:     // before propagating its typed error, so a subsequent `commit()`
      242:     // short-circuits with `BatchAborted` rather than persisting a
      243:     // partial batch (event durable, index marker missing).
      244:     //
      245:     // The `put_status_index` mirror test forces the failure by passing
      246:     // `IndexStatusState::Other(0)` to collide with the named
      247:     // `Submitted` variant; the `to_u8_checked()` guard inside
      248:     // `index_status_key` rejects the byte with a typed
      249:     // `JournalError::IndexStatusStateCollision`.
      250:     //
      251:     // There is no analogous discriminant on the action index:
      252:     // `index_action_key(action, run, step)` encodes a fixed
      253:     // `1 + 2 + 8 + 2 = 13` byte layout (1 prefix + u16 action + u64
      254:     // run + u16 step) into a 13-byte `ArrayVec`
      255:     // (`INDEX_ACTION_KEY_BYTES = 13` in `crate::constants`). For any
      256:     // valid `(ActionId, RunId, StepIdx)` input the `try_push` /
      257:     // `try_extend_from_slice` calls cannot overflow, so the
      258:     // `KeyCapacity` arm of `stage_pending_action_index_op` is
      259:     // structurally unreachable through the public API and the
      260:     // canonical `IndexStatusState::Other(0)`-style collision
      261:     // technique cannot be applied.
